
Here, we provide a practical demonstration of how to use the \hmetad{} package to fit the $\meta{d'}$ model in R. 

\subsection{Setup}
\subsubsection{Installation}
To install the latest release of the \hmetad{} package from CRAN, one can use the command \texttt{install.packages("hmetad")}. Alternatively, the development version of \hmetad{} can be installed using \texttt{devtools::install\_github("metacoglab/hmetad")}. 

The \hmetad{} package depends on the \texttt{brms} package, which in turn uses either the \texttt{Rstan} or \texttt{cmdstanr} interface to the probabilistic programming language Stan. Installing \hmetad{} will install \texttt{Rstan} automatically, however it is recommended to install the \texttt{cmdstanr} package, since it produces more optimized code for most applications. In either case, both interfaces requires a working C++ compiler. For detailed information on installation, please see \texttt{\url{https://mc-stan.org/install/}}. 

Once installed, the \hmetad{} package can be loaded using the command \texttt{library(hmetad)}.

<<echo=FALSE, results=FALSE, message=FALSE, warnings=FALSE>>=
install.packages("pak")
pak::pak("metacoglab/hmetad")
@


